            <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Image Blur&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;can use a camera which render to a rendered texture&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;add the images to be rendered to a second canvas, which uses the new camera with screenspace-camera&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Add blur shader to the Camera, or a parent object which contains all images&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Add the rendered texture to anywhere you like in the first camera&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamic Background Blur&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;http://answers.unity3d.com/questions/21699/unity-blur-behind-window.html&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&#xA;    &gt;Blur Behind Window&lt;/a&gt; Use Camera post effect&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;http://forum.unity3d.com/threads/solved-dynamic-blurred-background-on-ui.345083/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&#xA;    &gt;Dynamic Blurred Background on UI&lt;/a&gt; Use Grabpass&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;http://blog.ivank.net/fastest-gaussian-blur.html&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&#xA;    &gt;http://blog.ivank.net/fastest-gaussian-blur.html&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;</description>
